<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:AgIO.Views"
        x:Class="AgIO.Views.FormUDPMonitor"
        x:DataType="vm:FormUDPMonitorViewModel"
        Title="UDP Monitor"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        RequestedThemeVariant="Light"
        Background="White"
        Width="456"
        Height="291"
        MinWidth="456"
        MinHeight="291"
        CanResize="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        SystemDecorations="Full"
        FontFamily="Tahoma"
        FontSize="14.25">
    <!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms FormUDPMonitor.cs + FormUDPMonitor.designer.cs — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
    <!--
        [XPLAT] Avalonia 1:1 PARITY reimplementation of the deleted WinForms `Forms/FormUDPMonitor`
        (FormUDPMonitor.designer.cs + FormUDPMonitor.cs + FormUDPMonitor.resx) — the AgIO "UDP
        Monitor": a large read-only receive area that mirrors the live UDP loopback traffic, with
        Log / Log-NMEA / Log-NTRIP capture toggles, Clear, Save, a "Guide ->" link to the PGN
        reference window, and Close. Per AAP §0.3.3 this is a visual PARITY reimplementation of the
        original Windows Forms look — never a redesign. No Figma was supplied (AAP §0.8); the
        rendered WinForms dialog is the sole visual reference.

        Bound (compiled bindings, x:DataType="vm:FormUDPMonitorViewModel") to FormUDPMonitorViewModel.
        That view-model already replaced the WinForms `FormLoop mf` god-object back-reference and the
        333 ms drain timer; this view is purely declarative. The view-model's RequestClose /
        RequestOpenPgn / RequestTimedMessage events and Cleanup() are window-level concerns handled
        by the code-behind (FormUDPMonitor.axaml.cs), not here.

        Root-attribute parity mapping (WinForms FormUDPMonitor.designer.cs -> Avalonia):
          • Form Text "UDP Monitor"              -> Title="UDP Monitor".
          • BackColor White                      -> Background="White" (white receive area framed by
                                                    the window — matches the original).
          • ClientSize 456 x 291                 -> Width="456" Height="291" (initial size; the
                                                    sibling-view convention maps WinForms ClientSize
                                                    directly to Width/Height). The WinForms
                                                    MinimumSize (465 x 307 total, i.e. ~= the 456x291
                                                    client plus the thin tool-window border) means the
                                                    form opened at its floor and could only grow, so
                                                    MinWidth/MinHeight are pinned to the initial size.
          • FormBorderStyle SizableToolWindow    -> CanResize="True" (the original was resizable; the
                                                    receive box grew with it — see below).
          • MaximizeBox=false / MinimizeBox=false
            / ControlBox=false                   -> NOT reproduced: hiding only the title-bar system
                                                    buttons is not portable across Windows/Linux/macOS
                                                    and risks trapping the operator. SystemDecorations
                                                    ="Full" keeps a standard, usable frame; the dialog
                                                    is dismissed via the Close button (parity of
                                                    intent — matches sibling FormEventViewer).
          • StartPosition CenterParent           -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner".
          • Font Tahoma                          -> base FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="14.25"
                                                    (sibling-view convention); children override their
                                                    own sizes below.
          • RequestedThemeVariant="Light"        -> AgIO is light-only (App.axaml pins Light, no
                                                    day/night toggle); restated here for parity.
          • ShowInTaskbar                         -> "False" (a child monitor dialog, not a taskbar
                                                    window). The original was a non-modal monitor and
                                                    was NOT TopMost, so Topmost is deliberately unset.

        Buttons render as TEXT, not the WinForms OK64 / LogNMEA / VehFileSave / Trash / Nmea /
        NTRIP_Client bitmaps: the migrated AgIO.csproj registers NO btnImages assets as
        <AvaloniaResource> (only GPS/AgOpenGPS.csproj does) and excludes Properties/Resources.
        Designer.cs from compilation (System.Drawing purged), so an avares://AgIO/btnImages/*
        reference would not resolve and would render a broken image. Every migrated AgIO view
        therefore renders affordances as text — consistent with the sibling FormEventViewer /
        FormPGN / FormYes / FormSource and the agent-prompt's text-fallback path. See
        MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md.
    -->
    <DockPanel Margin="6" LastChildFill="True">

        <!-- Top header row — the WinForms static column headers over the receive log:
               lblSteerAngle "Time" (x=15), label1 "IP Address : Port" (x=100),
               label2 "PGN" (x=310), and the clickable lblPGNGuide "Guide ->" (x=381).
             "Time" + "IP Address : Port" form the left group; "PGN" + "Guide ->" the right group,
             separated by a star spacer (parity with the original left/right clustering). The three
             header captions are static (the view-model exposes no Time/IP/PGN values — the data
             they label scrolls inside the receive box), so they are plain TextBlocks; only
             "Guide ->" is interactive. Tahoma Bold 12 + near-black reproduce the WinForms labels
             (Tahoma 11.25 Bold, ForeColor ActiveCaptionText). -->
        <Grid DockPanel.Dock="Top"
              ColumnDefinitions="Auto,Auto,*,Auto,Auto"
              Margin="0,2,0,6">
            <TextBlock Grid.Column="0"
                       x:Name="lblSteerAngle"
                       Text="Time"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       FontSize="12"
                       Foreground="Black"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       Margin="9,0,0,0" />
            <TextBlock Grid.Column="1"
                       x:Name="label1"
                       Text="IP Address : Port"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       FontSize="12"
                       Foreground="Black"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       Margin="40,0,0,0" />
            <TextBlock Grid.Column="3"
                       x:Name="label2"
                       Text="PGN"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       FontSize="12"
                       Foreground="Black"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       Margin="0,0,8,0" />

            <!-- WinForms lblPGNGuide.Click -> lblPGNGuide_Click -> new FormPGN().Show(this).
                 Rendered as a flat, link-style Button (a clickable label is a real action, so it
                 is a <Button> for keyboard operability rather than a text element with a click
                 handler). Command -> OpenPgnCommand, which raises the view-model's RequestOpenPgn
                 event; the code-behind opens the Avalonia FormPGN reference window. The original
                 caption "Guide ->" is preserved verbatim. -->
            <Button Grid.Column="4"
                    x:Name="lblPGNGuide"
                    Content="Guide ->"
                    Command="{Binding OpenPgnCommand}"
                    Background="Transparent"
                    BorderThickness="0"
                    Padding="4,2"
                    MinWidth="0"
                    MinHeight="0"
                    FontWeight="Bold"
                    FontSize="12"
                    Foreground="#1B6FB3"
                    VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Right"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    ToolTip.Tip="Open the PGN reference guide" />
        </Grid>

        <!-- Bottom command bar — the WinForms bottom button row (all Anchor Bottom|Right), in the
             original left-to-right order:
               btnClear (Trash) | btnFileSave (VehFileSave) | btnLogNTRIP (NTRIP_Client) |
               btnLogNMEA (Nmea) | btnLog (LogNMEA, opens green) | btnSerialCancel (OK64, Close).
             Laid out as six equal-width columns so the row spans the dialog width and reflows
             cleanly on resize without overflowing (the original buttons were ~53px wide with ~18px
             gaps spanning x=6..451 of the 456 client). Heights are raised from the WinForms ~53 to
             a touch-friendly floor (Height 54, MinHeight 44 — AAP §0.3.3 "touch-friendly large
             controls"; sibling FormPGN/FormEventViewer use the same 44px floor). Each button is a
             text affordance (no System.Drawing imagery on this platform — see the header comment). -->
        <Grid DockPanel.Dock="Bottom"
              ColumnDefinitions="*,*,*,*,*,*"
              Margin="0,6,0,0">

            <!-- WinForms btnClear.Click -> btnClear_Click (textBoxRcv.Text = ""). -->
            <Button Grid.Column="0"
                    x:Name="btnClear"
                    Content="Clear"
                    Command="{Binding ClearCommand}"
                    Height="54"
                    MinHeight="44"
                    Margin="3,0"
                    FontSize="12"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    ToolTip.Tip="Clear the receive area" />

            <!-- WinForms btnFileSave.Click -> btnFileSave_Click (write text to zAgIO_UDP_log.txt). -->
            <Button Grid.Column="1"
                    x:Name="btnFileSave"
                    Content="Save"
                    Command="{Binding SaveFileCommand}"
                    Height="54"
                    MinHeight="44"
                    Margin="3,0"
                    FontSize="12"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    ToolTip.Tip="Save the captured text to zAgIO_UDP_log.txt" />

            <!-- WinForms btnLogNTRIP.Click -> btnLogNTRIP_Click (toggles mf.isNTRIPLogOn; BackColor
                 LightGreen on / Salmon off). Background bound to the view-model's NtripLogButtonBrush
                 so the toggle colour tracks state exactly (Brushes.LightGreen / Brushes.Salmon are
                 byte-identical to the System.Drawing colours of the original). -->
            <Button Grid.Column="2"
                    x:Name="btnLogNTRIP"
                    Content="Log NTRIP"
                    Command="{Binding ToggleNtripLogCommand}"
                    Background="{Binding NtripLogButtonBrush}"
                    Height="54"
                    MinHeight="44"
                    Margin="3,0"
                    FontSize="12"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    ToolTip.Tip="Toggle logging of NTRIP / RTCM traffic" />

            <!-- WinForms btnLogNMEA.Click -> btnLogNMEA_Click (toggles mf.isGPSLogOn; BackColor
                 LightGreen on / Salmon off). Background bound to NmeaLogButtonBrush. -->
            <Button Grid.Column="3"
                    x:Name="btnLogNMEA"
                    Content="Log NMEA"
                    Command="{Binding ToggleNmeaLogCommand}"
                    Background="{Binding NmeaLogButtonBrush}"
                    Height="54"
                    MinHeight="44"
                    Margin="3,0"
                    FontSize="12"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    ToolTip.Tip="Toggle logging of NMEA sentences" />

            <!-- WinForms btnLog.Click -> btnLog_Click (the master capture toggle; designer opened
                 green/LightGreen). Background bound to LogButtonBrush (LightGreen while capturing,
                 Salmon while stopped) — the view-model's IsLogOn setter starts/stops the drain
                 timer as it flips. -->
            <Button Grid.Column="4"
                    x:Name="btnLog"
                    Content="Log"
                    Command="{Binding ToggleLogCommand}"
                    Background="{Binding LogButtonBrush}"
                    Height="54"
                    MinHeight="44"
                    Margin="3,0"
                    FontSize="12"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    ToolTip.Tip="Start or pause capturing UDP traffic" />

            <!-- WinForms btnSerialCancel.Click -> btnSerialCancel_Click (mf.isUDPMonitorOn=false;
                 Close()). Command -> CloseCommand (runs Cleanup() then raises RequestClose; the
                 code-behind closes the window). IsCancel maps Esc to the close affordance for
                 keyboard parity (same pattern as sibling FormEventViewer's Exit button). -->
            <Button Grid.Column="5"
                    x:Name="btnClose"
                    Content="Close"
                    Command="{Binding CloseCommand}"
                    IsCancel="True"
                    Height="54"
                    MinHeight="44"
                    Margin="3,0"
                    FontSize="12"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                    ToolTip.Tip="Close the UDP monitor" />
        </Grid>

        <!-- Receive area — the WinForms `textBoxRcv` (read-only multiline TextBox, ScrollBars=Both,
             anchored all sides so it grew with the form). Reimplemented as a read-only multi-line
             TextBox that fills the remaining DockPanel space (LastChildFill, so it grows/shrinks
             with the window — parity with the all-sides anchor) and is bound to the running mirror
             of the drained UDP sentences. The TextBox carries its own ScrollViewer in its control
             template, driven here via the attached ScrollViewer.* visibilities (the idiomatic,
             sibling-view approach — wrapping a multi-line TextBox in an EXTERNAL ScrollViewer is an
             anti-pattern that breaks the caret/selection auto-scroll), so the text is scrollable as
             the agent-prompt requires.

             TextWrapping="Wrap" is set per the explicit agent-prompt directive; with wrapping there
             is no horizontal overflow, so the vertical scrollbar shows on demand and the horizontal
             one is disabled. ReceivedText is bound OneWay (the view-model property is get-only to
             the view: it has a private setter and a read-only control), which also avoids any
             compiled-binding write-back. The monospace font stack (Courier New first for
             Windows/macOS parity, then common Linux monospaces) preserves a fixed-pitch, readable
             log layout per the agent-prompt's "monospace ... readability parity"; FontSize 12 + Bold
             mirror the WinForms Tahoma 11.25 Bold weight. -->
        <TextBox x:Name="textBoxRcv"
                 Text="{Binding ReceivedText, Mode=OneWay}"
                 IsReadOnly="True"
                 AcceptsReturn="True"
                 TextWrapping="Wrap"
                 FontFamily="Courier New, DejaVu Sans Mono, Liberation Mono, Consolas, Menlo, monospace"
                 FontSize="12"
                 FontWeight="Bold"
                 ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                 ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" />
    </DockPanel>
</Window>
